# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-07-30: keep the PUBLIC tree to the METHOD -- the model, the data
# generator, the training loops, and the configs of the models we actually
# ship. Everything below is either bulk output, machine-specific operations,
# or paper/figure production: real work, but not what someone cloning this
# repo to use or check the method needs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# bulk artefacts
audit_rev*/
logs/

# internal working instructions for the agent, not project documentation
CLAUDE.md

# OPERATIONS: machine-specific orchestration for this one workstation
# (queue supervision, boot self-heal, thermal/stall watchdog). Hardcodes
# absolute paths, core masks and this box's failure history; useless and
# misleading anywhere else.

# EVALUATION AND SWEEPS: produce the paper's numbers, not the method

# FIGURE AND DOCUMENT PRODUCTION: renders the deck/paper, not the model

# ABLATION CONFIGS: the experiment record, not the shipped models. The two
# models this repo ships (Conv-ChArT, Conv-ChArT-FAST), their XSA variants,
# and the baseline they were cut from ARE tracked -- see configs/.
#
# GLOB + EXPLICIT EXCEPTIONS, replacing the hand-maintained deny-list (2026-07-31). The campaign
# now generates arms continuously via tools/cut_ablation.py, and a deny-list silently leaks every
# arm nobody remembered to add. Default-deny with named exceptions is the only version that stays
# correct as arms accumulate: to SHIP a config, name it below; everything else is experiment record.

# ABLATION TOOLING: cuts and verifies experiment configs. Useless once the arms are chosen.

# figures/ is DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED: paper/ is, so the conference
# deliverables (headline panel, pose table, cost table, architecture) are
# copied there to be pullable without the 295 MB of paper working files.

# figures/ removed from the public release (Kaelin, 2026-07-30). Conference
# deliverables stay local; they were purged from history, not just deleted, so
# they are not retrievable from an earlier commit either. Ignored here so a
# later `git add -A` cannot quietly put them back.
figures/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC TREE = DEFAULT-DENY (2026-08-31). The remote carries the METHOD only:
# the library, the four entry points needed to generate data / train / inspect,
# the conventions tests, and the deployment docs. Everything else -- evaluation
# and sweep tooling, figure and paper production, baseline arms, ablation
# configs, machine-specific operations -- is real work that lives locally and
# ships with the paper, not with the method.
#
# Default-deny with named exceptions, not a deny-list: a deny-list silently
# leaks every new file nobody remembered to add. To PUBLISH a file, name it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
configs/*
!configs/default.yaml

tools/*
!tools/audit.py
!tools/view.py
!tools/gen_eval_pose.py
!tools/gen_cutouts.py
!tools/train_detector.py
!tools/train_refiner.py
!tools/introspect.py

tests/*
!tests/test_synth.py
!tests/test_generator.py
!tests/test_model.py
!tests/test_pipeline.py
!tests/test_trainutil.py

docs/*
!docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
!docs/architecture.svg
!docs/TOOLING.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REPORT BRANCH (2026-10-09, Kaelin: "push all that out on a new branch called
# report ... for my honours thesis report - must be thorough"). Everything the
# public main tree withholds is re-included here: the paper, every results
# directory (READMEs, tables, JSON, figures, per-run logs), every config ever
# trained (the experiment record), the tooling that produced the numbers, and
# the conference deliverables. Later rules win, so these negations override the
# default-deny above. Still excluded: model weights and exports (*.pt, *.onnx,
# runs/, deploy/), generated image sets (eval_pose*/, sheets/, audit*),
# tools/charuconet.py (third-party MIT code, see above), LaTeX build files, and
# the rev-5 generator-audit overlays (8 x 12 MB sample sheets of a superseded
# generator revision).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!paper/
paper/conv_chart.aux
paper/conv_chart.log
paper/conv_chart.out
paper/results_rev5/07_generator_audit/overlay_*.png
!paper/**/logs/
!figures/
!configs/*
!tools/*
tools/charuconet.py
!tests/*
!docs/*
